       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (usually 850 mg TID). Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose, so it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg BID\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID with meals\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. I'd suggest pharmacy review in that case."
